# Linux AI

Linux-first AI chat app with tool-based computer access. Two front ends — a
Tauri 2 desktop app and a `lai` CLI — share one Rust core (`la-core`).

## Architecture

- `crates/core/` (`la-core`) — providers, tools, agent loop, SQLite store,
  config, transcribe. **All shared logic goes here.**
- `crates/cli/` — the `lai` binary (clap + rustyline).
- `desktop/src/` — Svelte 5 + Vite UI; `desktop/src-tauri/` — Tauri Rust shell.

Never duplicate provider/tool/agent logic into the CLI or desktop crates; call
into `la-core` instead.

## Non-negotiables

- **Naming**: product is "Linux AI", CLI command is `lai`. Never reintroduce
  "companion".
- **Security defaults**: mutating tools (`run_shell`, `write_file`, `open`)
  require approval; filesystem tools are confined to configured roots; shell is
  deny-listed. Don't weaken these.
- **Keys**: resolve via keyring → env → config. Never hardcode secrets.
- **Versioning**: git tag `vX.Y.Z` is the source of truth; the release workflow
  stamps versions. Don't hand-edit them.

## Scope guardrails

Not a local-LLM monolith, not an agentic coding tool. Keep it a lean app for
integrating AI into the Linux desktop.
